# Trip-line deadfall log (#363, D88), native 32x16: tied, strain, slip, swing, caught. The 24x10 log body sits at
# x 4-27, rows 5-14 (slip: one row lower); its two rope eyes are at x 8 and 23, row 4, where the game's ropes end.
# tied/strain/slip carry the pale lashing up to the bough. Palette of the sound branch plus end grain and bone cord.
